WEBVTT

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.950
I believed you, Nii-sama.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.870
That you would keep your promise.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:11.440
That you would be victorious 
and come back to me.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:13.820
So

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.810
you have to keep your promise.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.540
Satsuki.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.950
Your lips are like a kid's lips.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.980
Uh, who are you?

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.560
Your hurt's gone, right?

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.850
Principal.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:56.610
She just sent in mana from your 
lips to replenish what you'd lost.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.530
Then I just kissed...

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:07.990
Oh, Ranjou-san.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.390
I don't approve of illicit 
sexual relationships,

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:12.800
so I'm keeping her quiet for a while.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.260
I watched you fighting earlier.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.560
You're an Ancient Dragon, aren't you?

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.260
Huh?

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:22.890
The people of the Japan branch

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.770
of the White Knight Agency call 
it the oldest war dead spirit.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:27.770
The oldest?

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.990
Saviors are all reincarnates with past lives.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:35.250
It's been hypothesized for a long time

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.920
that there may be some Saviors that have

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.280
not one but two past lives.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.260
Wait a second.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.130
I'd finally remembered about 
my past life as a warrior.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.790
And now a second?

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.810
When you swung your sword 
down for your last strike,

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.260
you used the Step Three Dark Art.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.350
Anyway, you have no physical injuries.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.550
You're lucky you fought in the arena.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.150
Right.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.570
Go back to your dorm and get some rest.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.500
I'm reading poor fortune with women.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:12.980
You should be careful.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.140
Huh?

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:19.460
Don't forget to take this writhing 
classmate of yours with you when you go.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:20.600
Right.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.550
Flaga!

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:35.800
Thank goodness! You remember 
everything now, don't you?

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.670
No, not really everything.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.950
Oh, right, the promise!

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.890
Oh look, an ugly, washed-up octopus.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.730
S-Stop showing up out of nowhere.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.890
Moroha and I were about 
to have our promised...

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.020
Promised...

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.920
Kiss.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.820
Something like this?

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.450
Look, the octopus is boiling over.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:04.450
Hey, what are you doing to my Nii-sama?!

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.560
I knew it, ill fortune with women.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.340
Hey, Moroha, let's exchange phone 
numbers and email addresses.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.260
Can we?

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.570
Of course we can.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:46.090
Yay.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.370
Yay!

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:56.390
That's my third number, after Dad and Mom!

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:57.600
Dad and Mom...

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:01.360
Congratulations on your heart-wrenching 
level up, Ranjou-san.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.820
I get it, I'm a loner.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.820
I'm kidding. Trade with me, too.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:09.730
S-Sure, I guess.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:15.830
Shoot, my hand slipped. I deleted it.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.900
You want a fight, Urushibara?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.550
To the regular beauty shop, then.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.160
Is Haimura Moroha-kun here?

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.580
That's me.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.100
Could you come with me for a bit?

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.430
You, too, Urushibara Shizuno-kun.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.360
Rank C you say?

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.360
The principal recommended you, as well.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:47.990
And I watched your fighting in the arena.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:50.780
<b>3-2
Isurugi Jin</b>

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.320
My younger brother caused you some trouble.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:58.850
As a Rank C, you'll have some pay 
in the form of scholarships,

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:02.380
and you'll be guaranteed employment at the 
White Knight Agency after you graduate.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.880
But there are downsides.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.890
I see. You're not only 
strong, you're also smart.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.560
That's correct.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.890
When you become Rank C, you're required 
to become one of my Strikers.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.890
Strikers?

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:23.530
A real-combat troop of 
anti-Metaphysical fighters.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:26.820
You serve only once or twice a month,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.320
but there have been deaths in the past.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:32.170
You can have some time to think it over.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:39.520
So that pay, the scholarship, 
roughly how much do I get?

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.630
I-I did it, Auntie!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.480
You're content with that?

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:47.960
Looking forward to working with you, Senpai!

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:49.590
Welcome.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:52.960
I'll show up starting today, too, then.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:53.350
Huh?

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:58.850
We've been asking Urushibara-kun 
to join as a reserve.

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:00.850
See you after school.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.360
Let me in, too!

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.690
Um, who are you?

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:12.240
If Moroha and Urushibara are 
joining, I have to join, too!

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:16.720
I appreciate your enthusiasm, but I 
don't know anything about your ability.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.540
Her ability is enough for her to suffer 
a total loss against your brother.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.250
Urushibara!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:26.200
I think it's too soon for you 
to even the reserves.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:27.810
I'm sorry.

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.760
No way.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.300
Well, then.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:38.770
Hey, Satsuki?

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.810
I'm not upset or anything!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:46.110
I'm going to get stronger really 
fast, and I'll be standing

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.080
right next to you, seeing your back!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.600
Satsuki.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.830
I'll give a formal greeting.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:03.330
Welcome to the troop, 
Haimura Moroha-kun, Urushibara Shizuno-kun.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:09.870
Our third-years from last year graduated, 
so we're glad to have more forces.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.170
He's not bad-looking.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.340
I'll work you good, so be prepared.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:16.690
Okay.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.600
All right, let's begin.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:25.310
We are the swords of salvation.

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.120
We are the Saviors!

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:31.980
We are the strike for our people, 
our peace, and our justice.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:38.010
We are the strike for our people, 
our peace, and our justice.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:44.330
Do I have to shout that, too?

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:46.080
You should.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:48.590
Understood.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:50.780
All right, once more.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.860
We are the swords of salvation.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:54.550
We are the Saviors!

00:08:56.520 --> 00:09:00.470
Isurugi-senpai's generation is 
called the golden generation.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:06.310
They defeated more Metaphysicals 
than anyone in the Japan branch.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:10.190
So they're stronger than the adults 
in the White Knight Agency.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.740
Yes, most of them have surpassed Rank B.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:17.510
Can I really keep up in a place like that?

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.950
You'll be fine.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:24.540
I'm beat.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.750
I've never been so tired in my life.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:34.500
I know when to back off.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.260
You're late.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.800
My Nii-sama is the only person 
that can get away with

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.510
making me wait so long.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:44.020
I'm that Nii-sama, aren't I?

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:48.830
Hey, I found a good okonomiyaki shop.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.990
It's only 300 yen, in this economy!

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:52.520
Seriously?

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.030
Hey, let's go.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:58.280
Sorry, go alone, if you wish.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:09:59.530
Huh?

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:02.980
Moroha and I are both extremely tired.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:05.690
We want to hurry home and rest.

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:06.890
Well, I...

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:09.540
We're going to have exercises every day.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.440
I believe being rested and 
ready for the next day is

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.280
part of what you're being paid for.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.550
Okay.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:17.790
Sorry,

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:20.470
I should have known better.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.110
It's not your fault.

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:25.910
But we're going to be late 
every night from now on,

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:29.100
so I think we'll end up disappointing 
you, even if you wait for us.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:34.820
But can I call you guys to hang 
out on break days, at least?

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.950
You're very welcome, right, Moroha?

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.100
Like I said, I...

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.290
Okay.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.320
Hey, Satsuki.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.490
Why would you say something like that?

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:47.830
You want money that you 
earn yourself, don't you?

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:51.080
You adore Ranjou-san, too, don't you?

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:56.310
I just took that into consideration 
so you don't have to lose, either.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:57.530
That's not the point.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.790
I don't like the way you 
act like you're willing

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:03.500
to get your hands dirty for me.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.770
Thanks for backing me up.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:08.210
But keep in mind

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:12.230
that it doesn't make me happy 
to have a girl take crap for me.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:17.070
If anything, make me happy by smiling for me.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:19.530
Satsuki!

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:23.800
I thought you'd say that.

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:33.030
Urushibara's keeping up, but I...

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:36.750
Hello?

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.000
<i>Are you all right? 
You sound like you're crying.</i>

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:41.900
I'm not crying.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:44.050
Don't go imagining things.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:49.030
Oh man, pollen allergy this 
year is really brutal.

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:50.250
<i>Liar.</i>

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.100
<i>You're a wreck from crying.</i>

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.730
Don't talk like you can see me.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:55.910
I can.

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:07.120
Let's go have okonomiyaki 
or something during a break.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.620
You better make it good.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:14.380
I'll make okonomiyaki so good 
that you won't be able to

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.170
go on living without it.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:19.280
Hey, Satsuki,

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:22.930
is it all right if I keep calling 
you before I go to bed and stuff?

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:27.980
Y-You sure can't let go of 
your little sister, can you?

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:28.890
Fine.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:32.940
I'm busy, too, but maybe 
three times a week or so.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.750
Fine, fine. Three times a week.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.230
I appreciate it.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.400
Jeez.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.430
So early in the morning...

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.820
<i>Hello? It's me.</i>

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:54.110
<i>Can you go out with me for a bit?</i>

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:57.330
Sorry, there's already someone I like.

00:12:57.650 --> 00:12:59.840
<i>That's not what I meant!</i>

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:05.950
What a weird day.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:10.030
So why did you call me 
out to a place like this?

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:13.380
You said I'm very welcome if 
it's on a break, didn't you?

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:14.720
Did I?

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:18.570
Anyway, I want to get Moroha 
a present to congratulate him

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.890
on his promotion to Rank C.

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:22.780
So why do I have to come along?

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:27.470
Because I don't know what to get him.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.550
And I don't have much 
spending money this month,

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:31.950
so I thought maybe we could 
get him something together.

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.230
Goodbye.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:36.140
Wait.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:37.750
Good grief...

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:53.270
I can't choose.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.940
I'm tired.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:58.560
Sorry to drag you along.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:02.560
<b>Crêpes</b>

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.230
Did you know?

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.570
Sweets are good when you're tired.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:03.550
Huh?

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.320
Strawberry and banana would be fine.

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:08.500
What?

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:09.200
Goodbye.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.820
Okay, fine!

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.290
Here you are.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:18.990
It's good.

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:28.180
It won't rain, will it?

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:33.650
What's going on?

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:52.280
A Metaphysical?

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:05.220
Urushibara.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.020
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:23.360
<i>But</i>

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:27.810
<i>I'd be a failure of a sister 
to my Nii-sama if I ran now.</i>

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:33.940
Come, Arciel.

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:51.260
I'll be the one to fight you.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.760
You better thank me.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.260
Urushibara, take care of the kids.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.270
Ranjou-san, you can't take on it alone.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.910
I have to stop it here.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:08.530
That's right, you're up against me.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.760
Don't go cheating on me.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:24.920
Write.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.490
<b>Darkness of ice, spirit of snow, lend me your breath. 
Freeze them to a silence deeper than death.</b>

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:29.000
Freeze them.

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:35.430
Urushibara.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:38.720
I contacted the school and Moroha.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.680
The shoppers are being evacuated, as well.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:43.690
Then you go evacuate, too.

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:46.050
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:49.040
I'm the revered witch of the netherworld.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:51.860
I can support you no problem.

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:55.700
Dammit. I don't need your help, though.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:23.100
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:26.350
<i>Another one?</i>

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.900
You've got to be kidding me.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:36.950
It's hydra-headed.

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:40.910
This is hopeless.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:44.410
Satsuki!

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:47.690
My feet!

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:50.500
Raise your Plana and fight 
off the stone curse.

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:55.050
Bring it on.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.760
I'll take as many of you 
down with me as I can.

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:02.830
Are they enjoying this?

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:04.270
What do you think?

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:11.520
Moroha!

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.030
Tell me what's going on.

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:17.850
This is bad.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:19.710
They're as high-ranked as

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:22.450
the Metaphysicals that attacked 
Tokyo Bay, if not higher.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.910
There's never been one with nine heads.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.280
Then we have to send help quickly.

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:30.970
Satsuki and Shizuno are on the scene, too.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:32.310
We can't send help.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.770
It wouldn't be a match for us if 
it were an ordinary Metaphysical.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:41.180
But it's not one that we could win 
against without an army of a hundred.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:42.950
No way.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:44.930
Please understand.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:54.440
<b>Operation in Progress</b>

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.110
<b>Operation in Progress</b>

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:58.570
Dad! Mom!

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:01.670
Please, use my blood.

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.810
Save my Dad and Mom.

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:05.810
You're still too young.

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.650
You can't donate blood.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.340
No way.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:11.320
Please understand.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.090
Listen.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:18.700
There are no lives in this 
world that shouldn't be valued.

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.500
How can we call ourselves 
the swords of salvation

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:24.850
if we can't even save two girls?

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:30.390
Open your eyes, Urushibara.

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:31.520
Urushibara!

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:40.570
No!

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:43.910
Moroha!

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:48.410
<i>Nii-sama isn't going to 
praise me at this rate.</i>

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:54.340
<i>It's over.</i>

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:58.340
Saratiga!

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:09.560
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.060
Nii-sama.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.000
Dammit.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:42.720
These things...

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:50.350
It's okay.

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:52.600
You won't lose.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:56.270
You should have another power.

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:59.190
Another power?

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:01.520
You can do it.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:03.900
Don't hesitate.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.410
I remember.

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:20.890
I won't forgive anyone who takes from me!

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:22.330
Write!

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:25.540
<b>There exists purgatory in the netherworld and 
fields of fire in the corporeal world.</b>

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:31.630
<b>Fire discriminates not against good nor evil 
as it burns and purifies with ferocious mercy.</b>

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:29.980
More!

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:31.640
More!

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:35.630
<b>All must die and return to bone.</b>

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:34.600
<i>More! More! More!</i>

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:38.890
<b>God has forsaken humanity.</b>

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:44.890
<b>The world of the decadent is eternal. 
The trumpets must blare and bring the moment of judgment.</b>

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.640
<i>More! More! More!</i>

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.240
What is that?

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:55.250
Step Five Dark Art, Black Gehenna.

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:10.700
Yin Yang Kurikara!

00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:39.860
I was right about him.

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:47.380
In the reserves?

00:22:48.030 --> 00:22:52.910
You bravely challenged that monster 
and tried to protect the defenseless.

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:57.390
We want someone like you, with a 
true sense of justice, in the Strikers.

00:22:57.820 --> 00:22:59.400
We really want you.

00:23:00.390 --> 00:23:02.400
Me? In the Strikers?

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:05.400
And Haimura-kun,

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:09.410
I don't think my decision was wrong.

00:23:10.270 --> 00:23:11.410
But

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:15.270
I believe your decision was also correct.

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:17.960
You'll continue working for 
the Strikers, won't you?

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:18.910
Yes.

00:23:19.590 --> 00:23:22.540
All right, see you at the 
exercises after school.

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:26.910
Yay!

00:23:26.910 --> 00:23:29.180
I'm not left out anymore.

00:23:29.180 --> 00:23:31.220
We're together, Nii-sama.

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:32.540
I'm so happy.

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:34.520
Be careful not to drag us down.

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:35.580
Shut up.

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:39.470
I'll fix up your attitude real 
good. You'd better thank me.

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:44.570
Good grief...

00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:48.570
So by the way, what were 
we in our past lives?

00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:51.570
Let's talk about that later.

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:54.570
<i>Where do miracles happen?</i>

00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:57.120
<i>In the depths of a forest maze?</i>

00:23:57.500 --> 00:23:59.420
<i>Up high on a tall tower?</i>

00:23:59.890 --> 00:24:02.970
<i>Our miracles were right in front of us.</i>

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:06.270
<i>Our two past lives, our two memories.</i>

00:24:06.700 --> 00:24:09.670
<i>The more we remember, 
the stronger they become.</i>

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:14.350
Haimura Moroha-san, 
the oldest war dead spirit.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:24.850
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:15.560 --> 00:24:20.040
So, Moroha, my kiss or Maya-san's 
kiss, which did you like more?

00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:21.860
I don't remember any of it.

00:24:21.860 --> 00:24:24.040
Next time, "Witch of the Netherworld."

00:24:24.040 --> 00:24:25.050
Write!
